  "bodyText": "Skip to content\n\nIDEA\n\nInternational Development Ethics Association\n\nAbout\nOfficers Board\nBylaws\nPast Events\n \nMember Resources\nJoining IDEA\nYOUTUBE VIDEO LIBRARY\n\nPlease share with the webmaster any youtube videos dealing with development topics.\n\nA 2013 U.S. National Endowment for the Humanities Institute created teaching tools to aid K-12 teachers in their mission to educate students on important issues found under the heading of development ethics, including global hunger, human rights, development and education, global health, food justice and sovereignty, violence, government and development, and the Millennium Development Goals to name a few.\n\nVideos: http://nehinstitute.philosophy.msu.edu/?page_id=466\n\nEducational pages: http://nehinstitute.philosophy.msu.edu/?page_id=464\n\n \n\n6 Replies to “YouTube Video Library”\nSamantha\n2011-07-15 AT 00:56\nReport\n\nSamantha\n2011-07-15 AT 00:58\nReport\n\nSamantha\n2011-07-15 AT 01:01\nReport\n\nSamantha\n2011-07-15 AT 01:02\nReport\n\nSamantha\n2011-07-15 AT 01:07\nReport\n\nSamantha\n2011-07-15 AT 01:13\nReport\n\nLeave a comment\n\nFree Download: A comprehensive introduction to development ethics is now available online at no cost: Jay Drydyk & Lori Keleher, eds. The Routledge Handbook of Development Ethics. Routledge Press, 2018.\n\nContact: IDEA Secretary Jack Simpson, jh10j3s@leeds.ac.uk",
  "footerText": "Samantha 2011-07-15 AT 00:56 Report"
}